www.wiktionary.com/wiki/chutay"}, {"title": "Smart Definition", "url": "https://buenospanish.com/dictionary/chala/etymology"}, {"title": "Geneanet > Recursos > Apellidos > CHAY", "url": "https://es.geneanet.org/apellidos/Chay"}]}, "No source I found says that \"chayaco\" is a variant of \"ch'allay.\" The search did not return any page that mentions \"chayaco\" at all.\n\nThe closest material is the RAE's historical dictionary entry for \"achalay,\" an Argentine, Ecuadorian, and Peruvian interjection. It gives the Quechua origin as achallay, glossed roughly as \"how pretty, how good\" (Del quechua achallay `qué lindo, qué bueno'). The entry lists related forms, including achalau and achala, and describes the word as an interjection expressing admiration afectuosa o irónica.\n\nA separate paper by Julio Flor Bernuy traces the Spanish word \"chalaco\" to a Quechua root, chalwa, meaning fish, with variants challwa and tsallwa. It treats the word as a derivation through the agentive suffix -koq and does not connect it to \"ch'allay\" or \"chayaco\" (variantes challwa / tsallwa).\n\nIf you have a source for the chayaco claim, such as a specific dictionary or regional study, I can search for that directly."], "durationSeconds": 4.898418834, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01DGKXGtc16L7cuCpKMBg4cj", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
