VARIADOS/CHALWAKOQ CHALACO - Dr. Julio Flor Bernuy.pdf"}, {"title": "dle.rae.es", "url": "https://dle.rae.es/?w=chaye"}]}, "No result confirms that \"chayaco\" is listed as a variant of *ch'allay* in a Quechua dictionary. The search did not return a dictionary entry for \"chayaco.\"\n\nThe closest match is the RAE historical dictionary entry for *achalay*, an Argentine, Ecuadorian and Peruvian interjection of admiration. It derives from a Quechua word, achallay, meaning \"qué lindo, qué bueno\". That entry lists variant spellings including *achalai*, *achallau* and *achala*, but not *chayaco*. Its variants are also not labeled as ch'allay forms.\n\nOther results were unrelated. They covered the Quechua word *chay* (\"that,\" per Wiktionary), a Quechua-derived entry for *challar* (to sprinkle liquor on the earth), and a UNIFÉ paper on *chalaco*. That paper traces *chalaco* to a Quechua root meaning fish, not to *ch'allay*.\n\nA more targeted search of Quechua dictionaries such as Académico Diccionario Quechua or Diccionario Quechua-Español-Quechua, or of \"chayaco\" as a regional Spanish term, might settle the question."], "durationSeconds": 5.047266208000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_012xkhTRmn9m2kCbNJBPANYE", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
