es pleasure in Bolivia.\n- **achachay:** This interjection, of Quechua origin, expresses cold. The RAE's current entry also lists a use for fear in Peru. De or. quechua.\n- **quechua:** The RAE defines the language as one que hablaban los antiguos quechuas y que en la actualidad se habla en el Perú, Bolivia y zonas de Colombia, el Ecuador, Chile y la Argentina.\n\nThe results don't confirm whether \"chayaco\" or \"ch'allay y\" is an entry. A direct search of dle.rae.es for each term, or a check of the historical dictionary (dhle.rae.es), would settle it."], "durationSeconds": 5.887050457999998, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01PehVgB5gc2TMkboQs2LBcQ", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
